# One rule, for one file, and deliberately nothing else.
#
# ValheimBakaLoader/Resources/host/ValheimBakaLoader.exe is the frozen launcher, and the whole
# point of it is that its bytes never change: every release ships that exact file so a
# self-update writes no new exe and a virus scanner has no new hash to form an opinion about.
# A checkout with Git's Windows default, core.autocrlf true, rewrites line endings in anything
# Git thinks is text. Git's own heuristic calls this file binary today, because it is full of
# zero bytes, so nothing is broken; but a file whose entire value is its hash should not be
# resting on a heuristic. This says it outright.
#
# There is deliberately no repository wide rule here, no pattern matching every path. This
# repository has been checked out and committed under autocrlf for its whole life and its
# files carry a mix of endings; a rule over all of them would renormalise every file in one
# commit, which is a large diff saying nothing and a gate reading the wrong line endings.
# Keep this file narrow: one line per file that genuinely needs one.
ValheimBakaLoader/Resources/host/ValheimBakaLoader.exe binary
